#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:4
msgid "File Versioning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:6
msgid ""
"Syncthing supports archiving the old version of a file when it is deleted or "
"replaced with a newer version from the cluster. This is called \"file "
"versioning\" and uses one of the available *versioning strategies* described "
"below. File versioning is configured per folder, on a per-device basis, and "
"defaults to \"no file versioning\", i.e. no old copies of files are kept."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:13
msgid ""
"Versioning applies to changes received *from other devices*. That is, if "
"Alice has versioning turned on and Bob changes a file, the old version will "
"be archived on Alice's computer when that change is synced from Bob. If "
"Alice changes a file locally on her own computer Syncthing will not and can "
"not archive the old version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:19
msgid ""
"The applicable configuration options for each versioning strategy are "
"described below.  For most of them it's possible to specify where the "
"versions are stored, with the default being the ``.stversions`` folder "
"inside the shared folder path. If you set a custom version path, please "
"ensure that it's on the same partition or filesystem as the regular folder "
"path, as moving files there may otherwise fail."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:27
msgid "Trash Can File Versioning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:29
msgid ""
"This versioning strategy emulates the common \"trash can\" approach. When a "
"file is deleted or replaced due to a change on a remote device, it is moved "
"to the trash can in the ``.stversions`` folder. If a file with the same name "
"was already in the trash can it is replaced."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:34
msgid ""
"A :opt:`configuration option <folder.versioning.params.cleanoutDays>` is "
"available to clean the trash can from files older than a specified number of "
"days.  If this is set to a positive number of days, files will be removed "
"when they have been in the trash can that long.  Setting this to zero "
"prevents any files from being removed from the trash can automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:41
msgid "Simple File Versioning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:43
msgid ""
"With \"Simple File Versioning\" files are moved to the ``.stversions`` "
"folder when replaced or deleted on a remote device.  In addition to the :opt:"
"`~folder.versioning.params.cleanoutDays` option, this strategy also takes a "
"value in an input titled \"Keep Versions\" which tells Syncthing how many "
"old versions of the file it should :opt:`~folder.versioning.params.keep`.  "
"For example, if you set this value to 5, if a file is replaced 5 times on a "
"remote device, you will see 5 time-stamped versions on that file in the ``."
"stversions`` folder on the other devices sharing the same folder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:54
msgid "Staggered File Versioning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:56
msgid ""
"With \"Staggered File Versioning\" files are also moved to the ``."
"stversions`` folder when replaced or deleted on a remote device (just like "
"\"Simple File Versioning\"), however, versions are automatically deleted if "
"they are older than the maximum age or exceed the number of files allowed in "
"an interval."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:61
msgid ""
"The following intervals are used and they each have a maximum number of "
"files that will be kept for each."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:64
msgid "1 Hour"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:65
msgid ""
"For the first hour, the oldest version in every 30-seconds interval is kept."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:67
msgid "1 Day"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:68
msgid "For the first day, the oldest version in every hour is kept."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:69
msgid "30 Days"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:70
msgid "For the first 30 days, the oldest version in every day is kept."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:71
msgid "Until Maximum Age"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:72
msgid "Until maximum age, the oldest version in every week is kept."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:73
msgid "Maximum Age"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:74
msgid ""
"The maximum time to keep a version in days. For example, to keep replaced or "
"deleted files in the ``.stversions`` folder for an entire year, use 365. If "
"only for 10 days, use 10.  Corresponds to the :opt:`~folder.versioning."
"params.maxAge` option. **Note: Set to 0 to keep versions forever.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:80
msgid ""
"This means that there is only one version in each interval and as files age "
"they will be deleted unless when the interval they are entering is empty. By "
"keeping the oldest versions this versioning scheme preserves the file if it "
"is overwritten."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:85
msgid ""
"For more info, check the `unit test file <https://github.com/syncthing/"
"syncthing/blob/main/lib/versioner/staggered_test.go#L32>`__ that shows which "
"versions are deleted for a specific run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:90
msgid "External File Versioning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:92
msgid ""
"This versioning strategy delegates the decision on what to do to an :opt:"
"`external command <folder.versioning.params.command>` (e.g. a program or a "
"command line script).  Just prior to a file being replaced, the command will "
"be executed.  The file needs to be removed from the folder in the process, "
"or otherwise Syncthing will report an error.  The command can use the "
"following templated arguments:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:105
msgid "%FOLDER_PATH%"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:106
msgid "Path to the folder"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:108
msgid "%FILE_PATH%"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:109
msgid "Path to the file within the folder"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:111
msgid ""
"Note that the former expands to the path of the actual Syncthing folder, and "
"the latter to the path inside that folder. For instance, if you use the "
"default ``Sync`` folder in Windows, and the full path to the file is ``C:"
"\\Users\\User\\Sync\\Family photos\\IMG_2021-03-01.jpg``, then the "
"``%FOLDER_PATH%`` will be ``C:\\Users\\User\\Sync``, and the ``%FILE_PATH%`` "
"will be ``Family photos\\IMG_2021-03-01.jpg``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:119
msgid "Example for Unixes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:121
msgid ""
"Let's say I want to keep the latest version of each file as they are "
"replaced or removed; essentially I want a \"trash can\"-like behavior. For "
"this, I create the following script and store it as ``/Users/jb/bin/"
"onlylatest.sh`` (i.e. the ``bin`` directory in my home directory):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:126
msgid ""
"#!/bin/sh\n"
"set -eu\n"
"\n"
"# Where I want my versions stored\n"
"versionspath=~/.trashcan\n"
"\n"
"# The parameters we get from Syncthing\n"
"folderpath=\"$1\"\n"
"filepath=\"$2\"\n"
"\n"
"# First ensure the dir where we need to store the file exists\n"
"outpath=$(dirname \"$versionspath/$filepath\")\n"
"mkdir -p \"$outpath\"\n"
"# Then move the file there\n"
"mv -f \"$folderpath/$filepath\" \"$versionspath/$filepath\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:144
msgid ""
"I must ensure that the script has execute permissions (``chmod 755 "
"onlylatest.sh``), then configure Syncthing with command ``/Users/jb/bin/"
"onlylatest.sh %FOLDER_PATH% %FILE_PATH%``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:147
msgid ""
"Let's assume I have a folder \"default\" in ~/Sync, and that within that "
"folder there is a file ``docs/letter.txt`` that is being replaced or "
"deleted. The script will be called as if I ran this from the command line::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:151
msgid "$ /Users/jb/bin/onlylatest.sh /Users/jb/Sync docs/letter.txt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:153
msgid ""
"The script will then move the file in question to ``~/.trashcan/docs/letter."
"txt``, replacing any previous version of that letter that may already have "
"been there."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:158
msgid "Examples for Windows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:161
msgid "Move to a given folder using the command prompt (:abbr:`CMD`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:163
msgid ""
"On Windows we can use a batch script to perform the same \"trash can\"-like "
"behavior as mentioned above. I created the following script and saved it as "
"``C:\\Users\\mfrnd\\Scripts\\onlylatest.bat``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:167
msgid ""
"@echo off\n"
"\n"
"rem Enable UTF-8 encoding to deal with multilingual folder and file names\n"
"chcp 65001\n"
"\n"
"rem We need command extensions for md to create intermediate folders in one "
"go\n"
"setlocal enableextensions\n"
"\n"
"rem Where I want my versions stored\n"
"set \"versions_path=%USERPROFILE%\\.trashcan\"\n"
"\n"
"rem The parameters we get from Syncthing, '~' removes quotes if any\n"
"set \"folder_path=%~1\"\n"
"set \"file_path=%~2\"\n"
"\n"
"rem First ensure the dir where we need to store the file exists\n"
"for %%f in (\"%versions_path%\\%file_path%\") do set \"output_path=%%~dpf\"\n"
"if not exist \"%output_path%\" md \"%output_path%\" || exit /b\n"
"\n"
"rem Finally move the file, overwrite existing file if any\n"
"move /y \"%folder_path%\\%file_path%\" \"%versions_path%\\%file_path%\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:191
msgid ""
"Finally, I set ``\"C:\\Users\\mfrnd\\Scripts\\onlylatest.bat\" "
"\"%FOLDER_PATH%\" \"%FILE_PATH%\"`` as the command name in Syncthing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:195
msgid "Move to the Recycle Bin using PowerShell"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:197
msgid ""
"We can use PowerShell to send files directly to the Recycle Bin, which "
"mimics the behaviour of deleting them using the Windows Explorer. Firstly, "
"create the following script and save it in your preferred location, e.g. ``C:"
"\\Users\\User\\Scripts\\SendToRecycleBin.ps1``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:202
msgid ""
"# PowerShell has no native method to recycle files, so we use Visual\n"
"# Basic to perform the operation. If succeeded, we also include the\n"
"# recycled file in the Syncthing's DEBUG output.\n"
"Add-Type -AssemblyName Microsoft.VisualBasic\n"
"[Microsoft.VisualBasic.FileIO.FileSystem]::"
"DeleteFile($args,'OnlyErrorDialogs','SendToRecycleBin')\n"
"if ($?) {\n"
"  Write-Output (\"Recycled \" + $args + \".\")\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:213
msgid ""
"Alternatively, the script can be expanded to send only deleted files to the "
"Recycle Bin, and permanently delete modified ones, which makes it more "
"consistent with how the Explorer works."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:217
msgid ""
"# PowerShell has no native method to recycle files, so we use Visual\n"
"# Basic to perform the operation.\n"
"Add-Type -AssemblyName Microsoft.VisualBasic\n"
"\n"
"# We need to test if a Syncthing .tmp file exists. If it does, we assume\n"
"# a modification and delete the existing file. If if does not, we assume\n"
"# a deletion and recycle the current file. If succeeded, we also include\n"
"# the deleted/recycled file in the Syncthing's DEBUG output.\n"
"if (Test-Path -LiteralPath ((Split-Path -Path $args) + \"\\~syncthing~\" + "
"(Split-Path -Path $args -Leaf) + \".tmp\")) {\n"
"  [Microsoft.VisualBasic.FileIO.FileSystem]::"
"DeleteFile($args,'OnlyErrorDialogs','DeletePermanently')\n"
"  if ($?) {\n"
"    Write-Output (\"Deleted \" + $args + \".\")\n"
"  }\n"
"} else {\n"
"  [Microsoft.VisualBasic.FileIO.FileSystem]::"
"DeleteFile($args,'OnlyErrorDialogs','SendToRecycleBin')\n"
"  if ($?) {\n"
"    Write-Output (\"Recycled \" + $args + \".\")\n"
"  }\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:239
msgid ""
"Finally, we set the command name in Syncthing to ``powershell.exe -"
"ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File \"C:\\Users\\User\\Scripts\\SendToRecycleBin."
"ps1\" \"%FOLDER_PATH%\\%FILE_PATH%\"``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:243
msgid ""
"The only caveat that you should be aware of is that if your Syncthing folder "
"is located on a portable storage, such as a USB stick, or if you have the "
"Recycle Bin disabled, then the script will end up deleting all files "
"permanently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:249
msgid "Configuration Parameter Reference"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:251
msgid ""
"The versioning settings are grouped into their own section of each folder in "
"the :opt:`configuration file <folder.versioning>`.  The following shows an "
"example of such a section in the XML:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:255
msgid ""
"<folder id=\"...\">\n"
"    <versioning type=\"simple\">\n"
"        <cleanupIntervalS>3600</cleanupIntervalS>\n"
"        <fsPath></fsPath>\n"
"        <fsType>basic</fsType>\n"
"        <param key=\"cleanoutDays\" val=\"0\"></param>\n"
"        <param key=\"keep\" val=\"5\"></param>\n"
"    </versioning>\n"
"</folder>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:269
msgid ""
"Selects one of the versioning strategies: ``trashcan``, ``simple``, "
"``staggered``, ``external`` or leave empty to disable versioning completely."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:274
msgid ""
"Overrides the path where old versions of files are stored and defaults to ``."
"stversions`` if left empty.  An absolute or relative path can be specified.  "
"The latter is interpreted relative to the shared folder path, if the :opt:"
"`~folder.versioning.fsType` is configured as ``basic``.  Ignored for the "
"``external`` versioning strategy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:280
msgid ""
"This option used to be stored under the keys ``fsPath`` or ``versionsPath`` "
"in the :opt:`~folder.versioning.params` element."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:285
msgid ""
"The internal file system implementation used to access this versions folder. "
"Only applies if :opt:`~folder.versioning.fsPath` is also set non-empty, "
"otherwise the :opt:`~folder.filesystemType` from the folder element is used "
"instead.  Refer to that option description for possible values.  Ignored for "
"the ``external`` versioning strategy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:291
msgid ""
"This option used to be stored under the key ``fsType`` in the :opt:`~folder."
"versioning.params` element."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:296
msgid ""
"The interval, in seconds, for running cleanup in the versions folder.  Zero "
"to disable periodic cleaning.  Limited to one year (31536000 seconds). "
"Ignored for the ``external`` versioning strategy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:300
msgid ""
"This option used to be stored under the key ``cleanInterval`` in the :opt:"
"`~folder.versioning.params` element."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:305
msgid ""
"Each versioning strategy can have configuration parameters specific to its "
"implementation under this element."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:310
msgid ""
"The number of days to keep files in the versions folder.  Zero means to keep "
"forever.  Older elements encountered during cleanup are removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:315
msgid "The number of old versions to keep, per file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:319
msgid ""
"The maximum time to keep a version, in seconds.  Zero means to keep forever."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/versioning.rst:323
msgid ""
"External command to execute for storing a file version about to be replaced "
"or deleted.  If the path to the application contains spaces, it should be "
"quoted."
msgstr ""
